# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TumorNet 2000 — what is deliberately NOT published, and why.
#
# Two of these exclusions are not about repository size. Read them before
# removing anything.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── 1. THE DATASET — attribution is withheld, so we cannot legally redistribute
#
# agentic-medical-ai-lab/ is a SEPARATE upstream repository
# (github.com/kimmouridsen-cloud/agentic-medical-ai-lab). Its MIT licence covers
# the software; the imaging data carries its own terms:
#
#   "CC-BY-SA 4.0 - source, citation and full attribution published with the
#    course material after the lab"          -- data/cases/dataset.json
#
# CC-BY-SA *requires* attribution, and that attribution has not been published
# yet — the upstream repo gitignores ATTRIBUTION.md with the note "held back
# until the lab is over". We therefore cannot satisfy the licence by
# redistributing the data now. Clone the upstream repo instead; this project
# reads it from ./agentic-medical-ai-lab/.
agentic-medical-ai-lab/

# ── 2. THE EVAL SET — publishing it would leak a live competition
#
# The 60 eval cases are the test inputs of a private, currently-running
# classroom Kaggle competition: "Images only: no masks are published for these"
# (data/eval/tier_eval.txt). Republishing them — as NIfTI, as the browsable PNG
# atlases the web exporter produces, or as our own predicted masks — hands every
# other participant the test set or a ready-made answer. Excluded on fairness
# grounds, not size.
# Name-agnostic on purpose: an earlier pass excluded only `outputs/kaggle_eval/`
# and a sibling directory `outputs/kaggle_eval_backup_3donly/` walked straight
# past it carrying the submission and 60 predicted test masks. Match the CONTENT,
# not one directory name.
assets/cases/eval_*/
eval_*.nii
eval_*.nii.gz
eval_*_mask.nii.gz
submission*.csv
outputs/*kaggle*/
outputs/*eval*/
outputs/predict_selftest/
outputs/predict_scoretest/

# ── 3. Derived data — regenerable in one command, and large
#
# assets/cases/ is 819 MB of PNG atlases rendered FROM the dataset above, so it
# inherits the same attribution problem as well as being bulky. The viewer
# degrades gracefully without it (see the documented fallback at the bottom of
# src/viewer.js) and it is rebuilt with:
#     python -m ml.export_web --full --arch 3d
assets/cases/

# ml/cache/ is 3.2 GB of preprocessed .npy, rebuilt with:  python -m ml.data --build
ml/cache/

# ── 4. Model weights — 4.7 GB, over GitHub's per-file limit
#
# Individual checkpoints are 36-70 MB and there are 42 of them over 50 MB; two
# exceed the 100 MB hard limit. Attach the deployed 5-fold set to a GitHub
# Release or use Git LFS if they need to ship. The JSON results and training
# histories ARE tracked, so every reported number stays auditable without them.
*.pt
*.pth
outputs/**/*.npz
outputs/**/*.npy
outputs/predictions/
nnunet_tumordetect/

# ── 5. Environments and scratch
.venv/
.venv-nnunet/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store
*.log

# ── 6. Credentials — never, under any circumstances
kaggle.json
access_token
.env
*.pem
*.key
